@sumati3031-arista - Reviewed the change; no blockers from my side.

The fix looks correct for dualtor: `giaddr_ip` remains the relay identifier and is set to Loopback0 in dualtor, while outbound DHCP replies toward clients use the VLAN SVI as the L3 source. So keeping `DHCP_CHECK_GIADDR` on `giaddr_ip` and changing `DHCP_CHECK_SRC_IP` to `vlan_ip` matches the packet semantics. In single-ToR, `giaddr_ip == vlan_ip`, so this should preserve existing behavior.

CI is green, and the 202605 backport request is backed by sonic-mgmt issue #25393 with failure details.
